[86.959282, "o", "\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[G  \u001b[38;2;168;181;230mcheckout_latency.xml\u001b[39m. It uses \u001b[38;2;168;181;230mindex=demo_checkout sourcetype=checkout\u001b[39m and defaults\r\n  to the last 24 hours. The four panels are:\r\n\r\n  \u001b[2m•\u001b[22m \u001b[1mp95 latency\u001b[22m shows the 95th percentile of \u001b[38;2;168;181;230mlatency_ms\u001b[39m (about 482 ms over the\r\n    last day).\r\n  \u001b[2m•\u001b[22m \u001b[1m5xx rate\u001b[22m shows the share of HTTP 5xx responses, about 0.50%, with\r\n    \u001b[38;2;168;181;230mnumberPrecision\u001b[39m set to 2 so the value is not rounded to 0%.\r\n  \u001b[2m•\u001b[22m \u001b[1mLatency over time\u001b[22m shows the p95 in 30-minute buckets.\r\n  \u001b[2m•\u001b[22m \u001b[1mLatency by region\u001b[22m compares p95 across \u001b[38;2;168;181;230meu-west-1\u001b[39m, \u001b[38;2;168;181;230map-southeast-1\u001b[39m, \u001b[38;2;168;181;230mus-west-2\u001b[39m,\r\n    and \u001b[38;2;168;181;230mus-east-1\u001b[39m.\r\n\r\n  Approve this command and I will rerun it with \u001b[38;2;168;181;230m--yes\u001b[39m, then open the dashboard in\r\n  Splunk Web and confirm every"]
